SUMMARY:Before the Blueprint
DESCRIPTION:Where did the people living in the palaces get water from? What do the thick walls mean? And why are there so many courtyards? \nThis workshop brings participants and students of architecture together around a table to read drawings of Rajasthan’s forts and palaces. Through writing and sketching\, participants will uncover what these iconic buildings know about climate\, water\, and defence. \nDrawings are how architecture speaks to society\, a shared language of abstraction that clients\, builders\, and architects rely on. Yet the great forts rose without them\, shaped by craftspeople whose skill lived in practice rather than on paper. Participants learn to read that knowledge back out of walls\, courtyards\, and water systems\, one sketch at a time. \nPlease Note: \n\nParticipants should bring a notebook\, pen\, pencil and eraser.\nLimited to 30 spots.\n\nThis event is a part of the “Drawing Knowledge” exhibition\, exploring the intelligent architecture of imperial India. Find the full schedule here. \nIn collaboration with: \n    \nVenue: Library\n\n\nClimate Ingenuity Inside India’s Palaces\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScwCoWTw9GI9WZ4GXA2h_ZNTyElBV5E8mTDoeQQ7pwIvy3caA/viewform?usp=dialog)\n \n*Facilitators*: Meghal Arya\, Anitha Suseelan\n*Event Categories*: Architecture\, Workshops
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/before-the-blueprint/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Architecture,Workshops
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Thumbnail_CRARI2.jpg
