SUMMARY:The Sitar’s Journey in Melody
DESCRIPTION:\nAn immersive morning of sitar and tabla awaits. \nThis Hindustani classical concert offers a unique exploration of the instrument that stands as the backbone of the tradition: the sitar. It begins with a lecture-demonstration tracing historical roots\, structural design\, tonal acoustics\, and stylistic transformations over centuries. Following this is a full morning raga recital\, highlighting the rich aesthetic traditions and intricate rhythmic dialogues between sitar and tabla. \nFor both the seasoned connoisseurs and new listeners\, this session offers a deeper appreciation of the heritage\, craft\, and soul of Indian classical music. The sitar is not just a musical instrument\, but a living\, evolving canvas of Indian culture that bridges centuries of tradition with timeless acoustic mastery. \n\n\nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\n\nHistory\, Heritage and Harmony\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeazkpAIuS2F6w3HDnX0NXmJbJ1U734x4PKzu1SDedGa8ZSUw/viewform)\n*Performers*: Ramprapanna Bhattacharya\, Rahul Pophali\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-sitars-journey-in-melody/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail_TSJIM.jpg
