UID:97593-1794940200-1794945600@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Three Women and a Camera
DESCRIPTION:56 min | English | 1998 \nThe birth of a nation\, and the promises it left unkept. \nThis documentary screening follows three women photographers\, Homai Vyarawalla\, Sheba Chhachhi\, and Dayanita Singh\, across two very different generations. If a picture is worth a thousand words\, what stories can they tell about the state of our nation? \nVyarawalla\, regarded as India’s first woman photojournalist\, worked for three decades from the late 1930s\, and her pictures carry the optimism of a new nation. Chhachhi and Singh\, working decades later\, grapple with the complexities and undelivered promises of the post-independence era. Director Sabeena Gadihoke brings their concerns into conversation: representation\, the relationship between subject and camera\, and the limits and possibilities of still photography in India in the late 1990s. The film won several awards\, including second prize at Film South Asia\, Kathmandu\, in 1999\, and a Certificate of Merit at the Mumbai International Film Festival in 2000. \nThis screening is hosted as part of Art is Life: Elsewhere\, an offshoot series of programs hosted at partner venues across Bengaluru as part of the Museum of Art & Photography’s (MAP) annual festival Art is Life. \nImage Credit\nHomai Vyarawalla\, Delhi\, mid-1950s. Courtesy of Sabeena Gadihoke. \nIn collaboration with: \n \n  \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nA Nation through the Female Lens\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScvi-V0zwIsOvmTAFPkg6Udzbs0_L5S33m1Rhj1Wgso6yAz_A/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Filmmaker*: Sabeena Gadihoke\n*Event Categories*: Film\, Gender\, Photography\, Visual Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/three-women-and-a-camera/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Film,Gender,Photography,Visual Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail.jpg
END:VEVENT
