SUMMARY:State of Statelessness
DESCRIPTION:\n106 min | Tibetan with English subtitles | 2024 | India\, United States\, Vietnam \nThis film is the first Tibetan-language anthology to explore the lives of Tibetans in exile around the world. Through four stories\, the feature film explores heartache and nostalgia amid the realities of dislocation\, sans judgement or romanticisation. What does home mean to a people scattered across borders\, national constructs\, and generations? \nIn 1959\, 100\,000 Tibetans followed His Holiness the Dalai Lama’s escape from Chinese occupation into Dharamshala\, India. The Tibetan diaspora now spans the world\, from the United States to the Mekong Delta\, having integrated into new countries in unique ways. The film captures the pain of a scattered people\, and finds in it resilience and the unexpected bonds that form in strange lands. \n\n\nThe organiser will be present for an audience Q&A. \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\n\nA Tibetan-Language Anthology on Exile and Belonging\nFor Ages 12+\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc5-p0F2-9Zvvo1DedtEpA0KKVO_undkyyU6PshNkEhd9p1hg/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speaker*: Norpell Wilberforce\n*Event Categories*: Culture\, Film\, Language\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/state-of-statelessness/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Culture,Film,Language,Society
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail_SOS.jpg
