SUMMARY:The Sufi Way
DESCRIPTION:Language: English\, Hindi\, Urdu\, Punjabi\, Farsi\, Sindhi \nThis immersive presentation weaves together stories and songs to bring alive the thought\, practice\, and philosophy of Sufism. Drawing on the poetry and lives of Rumi\, Bulleshah\, Amir Khusro\, Shah Latif\, and others\, the performance asks: what does it really mean to walk the path of the heart\, to lose oneself in love? \nEach story leads into a song: Rumi’s love for Shams Tabrizi and his haunting verses for him; Khusro and his murshid\, Nizamuddin Auliya\, and the beloved Chhap Tilak; Bulleshah winning back the favour of his murshid and composing Tere Ishq Nachaya. Moving through these and other lives and songs\, the session offers a glimpse into the world of the Sufi path: love\, abandon\, humility\, joy\, intoxication\, and non-self. \nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Library\n\n\nSongs and Stories of the Sufis\nFor Ages 10+\nRSVPs will open on Thu\, Nov 12 at 6pm.\n \n*Performer*: Vipul Rikhi\n*Event Categories*: Faith\, Music\, Performing Arts\, Philosophy
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-sufi-way/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Faith,Music,Performing Arts,Philosophy
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnailrikhi.jpg
END:VEVENT
