UID:96739-1795347000-1795352400@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Visual City
DESCRIPTION:A city speaks in images all the time: in the signs\, statues\, posters\, and people we pass without a second glance. This talk draws on decades of documenting Bengaluru to show how much sits in the details of its visual culture. How do we look keenly at the images around us and find their meaning? \nOffered by a Bengaluru-based multidisciplinary artist whose work spans painting\, photography\, installation\, and artist books\, the talk turns close looking into a way of reading the city. A gesture\, a fragment\, or something left out can matter as much as what is captured. What begins as curiosity leads to revelation\, and ultimately arrives at a more empathetic way of observing. You may never see the city the same way again. \n\n\nFrom Looking to Seeing: Art and the Making of Meaning\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd2uZSLl0oSV94PTkQpJuoMwMkEmCpkjRdsZlFKquMnw7IOkw/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speaker*: Ravikumar Kashi\n*Event Categories*: Bangalore\, Media\, Visual Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/visual-city/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Bangalore,Media,Visual Arts
